// --- a block the agent decorated: markdown bold or a heading ---
// An agent writing markdown reaches for ** around a marker on its own. The
// scanner used to require the marker bare on its line, so a correctly closed
// ledger read as no ledger at all - and with deferral language present that
// produced a retrospective accusing the agent of not closing what it closed.

{"text": "Added the parser. The streaming path will come in a follow-up PR.\n\n**[COVERAGE CHECK]**\n- parser: done\n- streaming: blocked - the upstream API has no chunked endpoint (404 from /v2/stream)\n- docs: returned - you said you would write them", "expect": "miss", "why": "a bolded marker is the same block; decoration is not absence"}
{"text": "Shipped the schema. Left the migration as a TODO.\n\n## [COVERAGE CHECK]\n- schema: done\n- migration: blocked - the staging DB is read-only (permission denied on ALTER)", "expect": "miss", "why": "a heading marker is the same block"}
{"text": "The retry policy still needs tuning.\n\n**[COVERAGE CHECK]:**\n- retries: returned - you wanted to pick the backoff curve", "expect": "miss", "why": "bold plus a trailing colon"}
{"text": "Streaming comes in a follow-up PR. The skill asks for a `**[COVERAGE CHECK]**` at the end.", "expect": "hit", "why": "a decorated marker inside INLINE CODE is documentation, not a closure - the deferral stands unclosed"}

// --- a FENCED example of the block is documentation, not a ledger ---
// Showing the format is exactly what an instruction that teaches it must do,
// and what a message explaining the skill looks like.

{"text": "Streaming comes in a follow-up PR.\n\nThe format is:\n\n```\n[COVERAGE CHECK]\n- <part>: done - <check run>\n- <part>: blocked - <observed limit>\n```\n\nThat is the shape.", "expect": "hit", "why": "a fenced template is not a closed ledger - the deferral stands unclosed"}

// --- the part line's separator: the agent picks the punctuation ---
